  "worked_solution": "Let $p$ represent the profit on a single game, in dollars. Using the given probabilities, let's summarize this in a table. If $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(p)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $p$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[p] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{4})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{3}{10})+5(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{9}{10}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{5+10+18+20}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{53}{20} \\\\  & =2.65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit is $$\\,2.65.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
